Do not fold the app comb into the draft skill.
App comb: `skills/detangler-app`. Apply: `skills/detangler-app-apply`.

Use **Detangler** for the family. Say "drafts" or "the app comb"
when the variant is not obvious. Header lockup:
*A structural pass for drafts and programs that have been worked over.*
Hero may still use *Combs the whole draft or the whole program, not
single strands.* — that line is opaque next to the name alone.

The job is drafts **and** programs that have been **worked over** —
by one person, by several, and especially by an agent. A lot of
editing tangles references, argument, journeys, repetition, weight,
and (on a program) authority. Cutting or reordering is one cause,
not the product. Two combs. Do not fold them.

The **skill** is the product. An agent reads it and writes
`report.md`. npm ships the folders. There is no command-line comb.
Do not emit line-level suggestions in `report.md`.

Site and README speak as the product (Detangler / it). No corporate we.
No builder I. Same register as Smell Check: direct, no helper theater.
